From ee1805433e00e3709c8a9999f979e9a1c27dabe0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: useraccessdenied <useraccessdenied@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:08:34 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 12/24] usb: typec: zero the altmode descriptor in
 typec_port_register_altmodes()

desc was left uninitialised on the stack; only svid, vdo and mode are set before it is passed to typec_port_register_altmode(), which copies desc->mode_selection (a bool) and desc->roles. UBSAN on a KASAN/UBSAN debug kernel (realme GT Neo 2, qcom pmic-typec):
  UBSAN: invalid-load in drivers/usb/typec/class.c:658: load of value 128 is not a valid value for type 'bool'

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/usb/typec/class.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/class.c b/drivers/usb/typec/class.c
index 0595e8cb8..7bb491ddc 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/class.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/class.c
@@ -2613,7 +2613,7 @@ void typec_port_register_altmodes(struct typec_port *port,
 	struct typec_altmode **altmodes, size_t n)
 {
 	struct fwnode_handle *child;
-	struct typec_altmode_desc desc;
+	struct typec_altmode_desc desc = { };
 	struct typec_altmode *alt;
 	size_t index = 0;
 	u16 svid;
